<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chola Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chola, Cholas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chola Empire was a Tamil dynasty of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> that reached its height in the eleventh century. It built a powerful navy and extended its influence across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. Its raids on the ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> in the eleventh century severely weakened the Srivijaya Empire's control of maritime trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chola-empire.jpg" alt="Chola Empire" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikel3012 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chola_Empire_Map_(1).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The first chiefs known from inscriptions, Nripa Kama II in the early eleventh century and his son Vinayaditya, who ruled c. 1047–1098, were feudatories of the Western Chalukya Empire and fought in its wars against the <b>Chola Empire</b>, which then held the old Ganga country around Talakad.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hoysala-empire">Hoysala Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Pandyas were one of the three ancient Tamil royal lineages, named with the <b>Cholas</b> and the Cheras in the Sangam poems and in Ashoka’s inscriptions, and associated with Madurai on the Vaigai river.</blockquote><a href="/empire/later-pandyan-empire">Later Pandyan Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Strait of Malacca had been dominated by Srivijaya, centred on Palembang, until the <b>Cholas</b> weakened it in the 11th century, and by the end of the 13th by the Javanese Singhasari and Majapahit.</blockquote><a href="/empire/malacca-sultanate">Malacca Sultanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Pagan maintained contacts with Sri Lanka, and Anawrahta is recorded as sending Buddhist monks to King Vijayabahu I to restore the Sinhalese ordination after the <b>Chola</b> occupation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/pagan-kingdom">Pagan Kingdom · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the eleventh century the <b>Chola</b> king Rajendra I sent an expedition to the Ganges around 1021–1023 that claims to have defeated Mahipala I, and later the Kalachuris and the Chalukyas of Kalyani raided Pala territory.</blockquote><a href="/empire/pala-empire">Pala Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the ninth century Nandivarman III defeated the Pandyas at the Battle of Tellaru, but the Pandya wars continued until the Battle of Sripurambiyam, around 885, when Aparajita and his Ganga ally Prithvipati I defeated the Pandya king Varaguna II with <b>Chola</b> support, at the cost of Prithvipati's life.</blockquote><a href="/empire/pallava-dynasty">Pallava dynasty · Military</a></li></ul></section>
